    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q1', 1, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'easy', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'What is the indication out of the sentence: ''I gave him a piece of my mind''?', 'What is the indication out of the sentence: ''I gave him a piece of my mind''?', 'Appreciation', 'Warning', 'Greeting', 'Scolding', 'Appreciation', 'Warning', 'Greeting', 'Scolding', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) Scolding

Explanation: The idiom ''give someone a piece of one''s mind'' means to tell someone angrily and frankly that one disapproves of their behaviour.

Option a expresses praise, b a caution, and c a salutation. Only d expresses the rebuke conveyed by the idiom.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) Scolding

व्याख्या: ''Give someone a piece of one''s mind'' मुहावरे का अर्थ किसी के व्यवहार पर नाराज होकर उसे खरी-खोटी सुनाना या डाँटना है।

विकल्प a प्रशंसा, b चेतावनी और c अभिवादन है। मुहावरे में निहित डाँट का अर्थ केवल विकल्प d देता है।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q2', 2, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'easy', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'What is the meaning of the expression: ''Blue blood''?', 'What is the meaning of the expression: ''Blue blood''?', 'Polluted industrial waste water', 'Sap of teak wood', 'An aristocrat', 'A costly object', 'Polluted industrial waste water', 'Sap of teak wood', 'An aristocrat', 'A costly object', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) An aristocrat

Explanation: ''Blue blood'' denotes noble or aristocratic ancestry; it is a figurative expression rather than a literal description of a fluid.

Options a and b describe liquids, while d describes an expensive object. None denotes aristocratic lineage.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) An aristocrat

व्याख्या: ''Blue blood'' कुलीन या अभिजात वंश का सूचक है। इसका अर्थ किसी द्रव के रंग से संबंधित नहीं है।

विकल्प a और b द्रवों तथा d महँगी वस्तु का वर्णन करता है। इनमें से कोई अभिजात वंश का अर्थ नहीं देता।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q3', 3, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', '''He was hoist by his own petard'' refers to', '''He was hoist by his own petard'' refers to', 'He had problems as a result of his own plans to hurt others', 'He was high up on the pole', 'He would usually run away from trouble', 'He was indifferent to his surroundings', 'He had problems as a result of his own plans to hurt others', 'He was high up on the pole', 'He would usually run away from trouble', 'He was indifferent to his surroundings', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) He had problems as a result of his own plans to hurt others

Explanation: A petard was an explosive device. The idiom describes being harmed by one''s own scheme intended to harm someone else.

Option b is a literal misreading of hoist. Options c and d describe avoidance and indifference, neither of which is the meaning.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) He had problems as a result of his own plans to hurt others

व्याख्या: Petard एक विस्फोटक यंत्र था। यह मुहावरा दूसरों को नुकसान पहुँचाने की अपनी ही योजना से स्वयं नुकसान उठाने को दर्शाता है।

विकल्प b में hoist का शाब्दिक अर्थ लिया गया है। विकल्प c परेशानी से बचना और d उदासीनता बताते हैं; दोनों मुहावरे के अर्थ से अलग हैं।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q4', 4, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'easy', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'What is a Ballad?', 'What is a Ballad?', 'A novel', 'A historical narration', 'A popular story or folktale in verse', 'Musical comedy', 'A novel', 'A historical narration', 'A popular story or folktale in verse', 'Musical comedy', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) A popular story or folktale in verse

Explanation: A ballad is a narrative poem or song, often telling a traditional or popular story. The verse form is essential to the definition.

A novel is generally prose. A historical narration need not be verse. Musical comedy is a theatrical genre rather than a ballad.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) A popular story or folktale in verse

व्याख्या: Ballad एक कथात्मक कविता या गीत है, जिसमें प्रायः लोकप्रिय या लोककथा कही जाती है। इसकी पद्यात्मक रचना मुख्य विशेषता है।

उपन्यास सामान्यतः गद्य होता है। ऐतिहासिक विवरण का पद्य होना आवश्यक नहीं है। संगीतमय हास्य-नाटक एक अलग नाट्य-विधा है।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q5', 5, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'easy', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Plagiarism means', 'Plagiarism means', 'There was an epidemic of plague in the area', 'It is a sort of political philosophy', 'It indicates a happy community spirit like in playing Holi', 'It is presenting the work of someone else as one''s own', 'There was an epidemic of plague in the area', 'It is a sort of political philosophy', 'It indicates a happy community spirit like in playing Holi', 'It is presenting the work of someone else as one''s own', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) It is presenting the work of someone else as one''s own

Explanation: Plagiarism is passing off another person''s work or ideas as one''s own without appropriate acknowledgment.

The similarity between plagiarism and plague does not establish a connection. Neither political philosophy nor festive community spirit defines plagiarism.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) It is presenting the work of someone else as one''s own

व्याख्या: Plagiarism का अर्थ किसी अन्य व्यक्ति की रचना या विचारों को उचित श्रेय दिए बिना अपना बताना है।

Plagiarism और plague की वर्तनी में समानता से अर्थ समान नहीं हो जाता। राजनीतिक दर्शन और उत्सव की सामुदायिक भावना भी इसका अर्थ नहीं हैं।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
