    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q9', 9, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'easy', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Consider the statement: ''The message of peace and brotherhood permeated the address by the Chief Guest.'' What is meant by ''permeate'' in this statement?', 'Consider the statement: ''The message of peace and brotherhood permeated the address by the Chief Guest.'' What is meant by ''permeate'' in this statement?', 'To advocate', 'To spread all over', 'To anchor and stabilize', 'To leave a permanent impression', 'To advocate', 'To spread all over', 'To anchor and stabilize', 'To leave a permanent impression', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) To spread all over

Explanation: Permeate means to spread throughout or pervade something. Peace and brotherhood were present throughout the address.

Advocate means support, anchor means fix firmly, and leave a permanent impression means create a lasting effect. These do not mean pervade throughout.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) To spread all over

व्याख्या: Permeate का अर्थ किसी चीज में सर्वत्र फैल जाना या व्याप्त होना है। शांति और भाईचारे का संदेश पूरे भाषण में व्याप्त था।

Advocate समर्थन करना, anchor स्थिर करना और permanent impression स्थायी प्रभाव छोड़ना है। इनमें से कोई सर्वत्र व्याप्त होने का अर्थ नहीं देता।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q10', 10, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Directions: The following ten (10) items (items 1 to 10) are on English Language; therefore, these items do not have Hindi Version.', 'Arrange the following to form a grammatically correct sentence:
