    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q51', 51, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.parliament_state_legislatures.structure_composition', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'easy', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'The term ''Dear Money'' refers to', 'महँगी मुद्रा (Dear Money) का अर्थ क्या है?', 'Low housing-loan interest rate', 'Value of money at the recession stage', 'High rate of interest', 'Savings from a reduction in housing-loan interest', 'आवास ऋण की कम ब्याज दर', 'मंदी में मुद्रा का मूल्य', 'ऊँची ब्याज दर', 'आवास ऋण की ब्याज दर घटने से बचत', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) High rate of interest

Explanation: Dear money means credit is expensive because interest rates are high.

Options a and d concern cheaper borrowing. Recession alone in b does not define expensive credit.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) ऊँची ब्याज दर

व्याख्या: महँगी मुद्रा का अर्थ ऊँची ब्याज दर के कारण ऋण महँगा होना है।

a और d सस्ते ऋण से संबंधित हैं। b में केवल मंदी महँगे ऋण की परिभाषा नहीं देती।

