    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q58', 58, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.parliament_state_legislatures.structure_composition', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Which statements about IMF are correct?
1. India is a founder member.
2. India’s quota is more than 4%.
3. The Finance Minister represents India ex officio.
4. IMF reviews India’s economy under Article IV.', 'IMF के संबंध में कौन-से कथन सही हैं?
1. भारत संस्थापक सदस्य है।
2. भारत का कोटा 4% से अधिक है।
3. वित्त मंत्री पदेन प्रतिनिधित्व करता है।
4. अनुच्छेद IV के अंतर्गत भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था की समीक्षा होती है।', '1, 2 and 3 only', '1, 3 and 4 only', '2 and 4 only', '1, 2, 3 and 4', 'केवल 1, 2 और 3', 'केवल 1, 3 और 4', 'केवल 2 और 4', '1, 2, 3 और 4', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) 1, 3 and 4 only

Explanation: India is an original IMF member, its Finance Minister serves as Governor, and Article IV consultations assess economic conditions. India’s quota share was below 4%.

Statements 1, 3 and 4 are correct. Every option containing statement 2 includes an incorrect quota claim.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) केवल 1, 3 और 4

