    ('epfo-apfc-2016-q86', 86, 2016, 'January', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.parliament_state_legislatures.structure_composition', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'easy', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Communication can occur in both directions, but only one direction at a time. What is it called?', 'संचार दोनों दिशाओं में हो सकता है, पर एक समय में एक ही दिशा में। इसे क्या कहते हैं?', 'Duplex', 'Half Duplex', 'Full Duplex', 'Simplex', 'Duplex', 'Half Duplex', 'Full Duplex', 'Simplex', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) Half Duplex

Explanation: Half duplex permits two-way communication alternately; full duplex permits simultaneous communication in both directions.

Simplex is one-way. Duplex alone is a general term; half duplex specifies the one-direction-at-a-time condition.

