Explanation: Reluctant means unwilling or hesitant; eager means keen and willing.

Anxious and happy express emotions. Unwilling is a synonym of reluctant, not its opposite.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) Eager

व्याख्या: Reluctant अनिच्छुक या हिचकिचाने वाला और eager उत्सुक तथा इच्छुक है।

Anxious और happy भावनाएँ बताते हैं। Unwilling reluctant का समानार्थी है, विलोम नहीं।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2017-q6', 6, 2017, 'February', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'easy', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions: Part A (questions 1–20) is on English language and is provided in English only.', 'Directions: Part A (questions 1–20) is on English language and is provided in English only.', 'Which one of the following is the antonym of the word written in capital letters in the sentence, “I cannot comply with the QUEER regulations of your land”?', 'Which one of the following is the antonym of the word written in capital letters in the sentence, “I cannot comply with the QUEER regulations of your land”?', 'Strange', 'Nimble', 'Everyday', 'Customary', 'Strange', 'Nimble', 'Everyday', 'Customary', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) Customary

Explanation: Queer here means unusual or strange. Customary means usual or conventional and best contrasts with unusual regulations.

Strange is a synonym; nimble means agile. Everyday refers to routine use, whereas customary most naturally describes ordinary regulations.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) Customary

व्याख्या: यहाँ queer असामान्य या विचित्र है। Customary सामान्य प्रथा के अनुरूप है और उपयुक्त विलोम है।

Strange समानार्थी और nimble फुर्तीला है। Everyday दैनिक उपयोग बताता है; regulations के संदर्भ में customary अधिक उपयुक्त है।

