    ('epfo-eoao-2017-q50', 50, 2017, 'February', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.parliament_state_legislatures.structure_composition', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Which one of the following countries is not a member of WTO?', 'इनमें से कौन-सा देश विश्व व्यापार संगठन का सदस्य नहीं है?', 'Japan', 'China', 'Iran', 'Russia', 'जापान', 'चीन', 'ईरान', 'रूस', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) Iran

Explanation: At the February 2017 exam, Iran was not a WTO member. China joined in 2001 and Russia in 2012; Japan was already a member.

Options a, b and d are WTO members at the relevant date. Iran’s observer/accession status did not amount to membership.

