    ('epfo-eoao-2017-q63', 63, 2017, 'February', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'general_accounting_principles.financial_statements_and_adjustments.capital_and_revenue_expenditure_and_receipts', 'General Accounting Principles', 'सामान्य लेखा सिद्धांत', 'Financial Statements, Depreciation & Adjustments', 'Financial Statements, Depreciation & Adjustments', 'Capital vs Revenue Expenditure & Receipts', 'Capital vs Revenue Expenditure & Receipts', 'medium', ARRAY['Capital vs Revenue', 'Expenditure & Receipts']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Legacies are generally', 'वसीयत से प्राप्त दान सामान्यतः कैसे दर्ज होता है?', 'Capitalized and taken to Balance Sheet', 'Treated as income', 'Treated as expenditure', 'Capitalized and taken to Suspense Account', 'पूँजीकृत करके तुलन-पत्र में', 'आय के रूप में', 'व्यय के रूप में', 'पूँजीकृत करके उचंत खाते में', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) Capitalized and taken to Balance Sheet

Explanation: A substantial legacy received by a nonprofit is traditionally treated as a capital receipt and included in its balance sheet rather than ordinary recurring income.

It is not an expense or an unexplained suspense item. A small legacy can be treated differently by policy, but the question asks the general convention.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) पूँजीकृत करके तुलन-पत्र में

व्याख्या: गैर-लाभकारी संस्था को वसीयत से मिली पर्याप्त राशि परंपरागत रूप से पूँजीगत प्राप्ति मानकर तुलन-पत्र में ली जाती है, सामान्य आवर्ती आय में नहीं।

यह व्यय या अस्पष्ट उचंत मद नहीं है। छोटी राशि का नीति-अनुसार अलग उपचार संभव है, पर प्रश्न सामान्य परंपरा का है।

उत्तर-कुंजी तुलना: स्वतंत्र उत्तर बाहरी स्रोत पर उपलब्ध UPSC के नाम से प्रकाशित श्रृंखला A की कुंजी से मेल खाता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2017-q64', 64, 2017, 'February', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'general_accounting_principles.special_and_advanced_accounts.consignment_and_joint_ventures', 'General Accounting Principles', 'सामान्य लेखा सिद्धांत', 'Special & Advanced Accounting Topics', 'Special & Advanced Accounting Topics', 'Consignment Accounts & Joint Ventures', 'Consignment Accounts & Joint Ventures', 'medium', ARRAY['Consignment Accounts', 'Joint Ventures']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'The abnormal loss on consignment is credited to', 'प्रेषण पर असामान्य हानि किस खाते में जमा की जाती है?', 'Profit and Loss Account', 'Consignee’s Account', 'Consignment Account', 'Income and Expenditure Account', 'लाभ-हानि खाता', 'प्रेषिती का खाता', 'प्रेषण खाता', 'आय-व्यय खाता', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) Consignment Account

Explanation: The abnormal-loss account is debited and the consignment account credited, removing abnormal loss from consignment trading results.

It is subsequently dealt with through recovery and profit/loss, but the credit in the initial abnormal-loss transfer is to the consignment account.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) प्रेषण खाता

