    ('epfo-eoao-2017-q119', 119, 2017, 'February', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.parliament_state_legislatures.structure_composition', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Parliament & State Legislatures', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'Structure & Composition (Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, Vidhan Sabha, Vidhan Parishad; Qualification & Disqualification - Article 102, Representation of the People Act 1951, Anti-Defection Law / 10th Schedule)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Three persons A, B and C run a business together and their shares are 17%, 37% and 46% respectively. Any profit they earn is distributed according to the proportion of their shares. If the difference of the profits of B and A on a given date is ₹1,000, what is the profit of C on that day?', 'A, B और C की व्यावसायिक हिस्सेदारी 17%, 37% और 46% है। B और A के लाभ का अंतर ₹1,000 हो तो C का लाभ कितना है?', '₹2,300', '₹2,350', '₹2,450', '₹4,600', '₹2,300', '₹2,350', '₹2,450', '₹4,600', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) ₹2,300

Explanation: The difference is 37%−17%=20% of total profit. Total profit = 1000/0.20 = 5000; C receives 46%×5000 = 2300.

The other amounts do not represent 46% of the implied ₹5,000 total profit.

Answer-key comparison: The independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series A key.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) ₹2,300

व्याख्या: अंतर कुल लाभ का 37%−17%=20% है। कुल लाभ 1000/0.20 = 5000 और C का भाग 46%×5000 = 2300 है।

अन्य राशियाँ प्राप्त ₹5,000 कुल लाभ का 46% नहीं हैं।

