    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q3', 3, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 1–5: Each sentence has three parts (a), (b) and (c). Select the part containing an error in grammar, usage or idiom. Select (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 1–5: Each sentence has three parts (a), (b) and (c). Select the part containing an error in grammar, usage or idiom. Select (d) if there is no error.', 'The book is well printed and attractively bound making altogether an attractive volume.', 'The book is well printed and attractively bound making altogether an attractive volume.', 'The book is well printed and attractively bound', 'making altogether', 'an attractive volume', 'No error', 'The book is well printed and attractively bound', 'making altogether', 'an attractive volume', 'No error', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) No error

Explanation: The participial phrase gives the overall result of the printing and binding; altogether means on the whole.

The coordination in a and construction in b–c are acceptable. Improved punctuation would not establish an error in a listed segment.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) No error

व्याख्या: Participial phrase छपाई और जिल्द का समग्र परिणाम बताता है; altogether का अर्थ कुल मिलाकर है।

a का संयोजन और b–c की रचना स्वीकार्य हैं। बेहतर विराम-चिह्न संभव हैं, पर इससे किसी विकल्प में आवश्यक त्रुटि नहीं बनती।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q4', 4, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 1–5: Each sentence has three parts (a), (b) and (c). Select the part containing an error in grammar, usage or idiom. Select (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 1–5: Each sentence has three parts (a), (b) and (c). Select the part containing an error in grammar, usage or idiom. Select (d) if there is no error.', 'A little younger to myself we, both were devoted to cricket and boating.', 'A little younger to myself we, both were devoted to cricket and boating.', 'A little younger', 'to myself we, both were', 'devoted to cricket and boating', 'No error', 'A little younger', 'to myself we, both were', 'devoted to cricket and boating', 'No error', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) to myself we, both were

Explanation: Younger takes than, not to. The segment also needs a coherent subject reference; “A little younger than I, he ...” is a possible correction.

The erroneous comparative preposition is in b. Parts a and c do not contain that error, excluding d.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) to myself we, both were

व्याख्या: Younger के साथ than आता है, to नहीं। कर्ता-संदर्भ भी संगत होना चाहिए; “A little younger than I, he ...” संभावित सुधार है।

गलत तुलनात्मक पूर्वसर्ग b में है। a और c में यह त्रुटि नहीं है; d सही नहीं है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q5', 5, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 1–5: Each sentence has three parts (a), (b) and (c). Select the part containing an error in grammar, usage or idiom. Select (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 1–5: Each sentence has three parts (a), (b) and (c). Select the part containing an error in grammar, usage or idiom. Select (d) if there is no error.', 'He had no sooner arrived than he was asked to leave again.', 'He had no sooner arrived than he was asked to leave again.', 'He had no sooner', 'arrived than', 'he was asked to leave again', 'No error', 'He had no sooner', 'arrived than', 'he was asked to leave again', 'No error', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) No error

Explanation: No sooner ... than is the correct correlative construction.

Past perfect in the first clause and past passive in the second correctly express the immediate succession; a–c are grammatical.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) No error

व्याख्या: No sooner ... than सही संबंध-सूचक रचना है।

पहले past perfect और दूसरे past passive से तत्काल क्रम सही व्यक्त है; a–c व्याकरणतः सही हैं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q6', 6, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 6–8: Select the most suitable word to fill in the blank.', 'Directions for questions 6–8: Select the most suitable word to fill in the blank.', 'The Rajputs always fought ___ the last man.', 'The Rajputs always fought ___ the last man.', 'upto', 'till', 'to', 'for', 'upto', 'till', 'to', 'for', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) to

Explanation: The fixed expression fight to the last man means continuing the struggle until none remain.

