    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q8', 8, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 6–8: Select the most suitable word to fill in the blank.', 'Directions for questions 6–8: Select the most suitable word to fill in the blank.', 'You should be considerate ___ your employees and I assure you of your success in every walk of life.', 'You should be considerate ___ your employees and I assure you of your success in every walk of life.', 'for', 'to', 'upon', 'on', 'for', 'to', 'upon', 'on', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) to

Explanation: Considerate to someone means thoughtful toward them. Considerate of is also standard, but of is not offered.

