Passage:
When you buy a car, examine carefully the important features of the model you are considering. Many a buyer of the latest models has got into trouble by buying a car too broad or too long for his garage. Furthermore, a long car is much harder to manoeuvre in traffic and much more difficult to park. Another important feature is the comfort afforded. Are the seats nice and durably upholstered? Is there enough glass area to give the driver a good view in all directions, particularly to the rear? It should be remembered that the heavier and more powerful a car is, the more expensive it will be to operate. High powered motors require expensive high-octane petrol. The greater weight means greater tyre wear and enlarged brakes. The old cliché is still true; it is not the initial cost but the upkeep which matters!', 'While buying a new car, one should specially consider its', 'While buying a new car, one should specially consider its', 'price', 'maintenance cost', 'upholstery', 'brakes', 'price', 'maintenance cost', 'upholstery', 'brakes', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) maintenance cost

Explanation: The conclusion expressly says upkeep matters more than initial cost.

Upholstery and brakes are individual features; price is the initial expense contrasted with continuing upkeep.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) maintenance cost

व्याख्या: अंतिम वाक्य आरंभिक लागत से रखरखाव को अधिक महत्त्व देता है।

जिल्द और ब्रेक अलग विशेषताएँ हैं; मूल्य आरंभिक व्यय है, निरंतर रखरखाव नहीं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q24', 24, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'I rather like the QUAINT little house at the end of the street.', 'I rather like the QUAINT little house at the end of the street.', 'old', 'quiet', 'unusual', 'haunted', 'old', 'quiet', 'unusual', 'haunted', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) unusual

Explanation: Quaint means attractively unusual or old-fashioned; unusual is the closest choice.

A house can be old without being quaint. Quiet and haunted do not define quaint.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) unusual

व्याख्या: Quaint आकर्षक रूप से अनोखा या पुराने ढंग का है; unusual निकटतम है।

घर पुराना होकर भी quaint नहीं हो सकता। Quiet और haunted इसका अर्थ नहीं हैं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q25', 25, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'If she continues to spend her time in such a FRIVOLOUS manner, she will fail in her examinations.', 'If she continues to spend her time in such a FRIVOLOUS manner, she will fail in her examinations.', 'frightful', 'leisurely', 'non-serious', 'calculated', 'frightful', 'leisurely', 'non-serious', 'calculated', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) non-serious

Explanation: Frivolous means lacking seriousness or sensible purpose.

Leisurely concerns pace, frightful fear and calculated planning, rather than lack of seriousness.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) non-serious

व्याख्या: Frivolous गंभीरता या उचित उद्देश्य का अभाव है।

Leisurely गति, frightful भय और calculated योजना से जुड़े हैं, गंभीरता के अभाव से नहीं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q26', 26, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'SANGUINE as he is in his attitude to life and its problems, he cannot but be noticed wherever he goes.', 'SANGUINE as he is in his attitude to life and its problems, he cannot but be noticed wherever he goes.', 'optimistic', 'enthusiastic', 'realistic', 'dispassionate', 'optimistic', 'enthusiastic', 'realistic', 'dispassionate', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) optimistic

Explanation: Sanguine means confident and optimistic about outcomes.

Enthusiastic means eager, realistic practical, and dispassionate unemotional; optimistic is precise.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) optimistic

व्याख्या: Sanguine परिणामों के बारे में आत्मविश्वासी और आशावादी है।

Enthusiastic उत्साही, realistic यथार्थवादी और dispassionate भावनारहित है; optimistic सटीक है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q27', 27, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'Directions for questions 24–27: Select the option nearest in meaning to the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'One’s REMONSTRATION against social ills has to be consistent to be fruitful.', 'One’s REMONSTRATION against social ills has to be consistent to be fruitful.', 'outrage', 'demonstration', 'protest', 'criticism', 'outrage', 'demonstration', 'protest', 'criticism', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) protest

Explanation: Remonstration is an earnest expression of protest or objection.

Outrage is emotion, demonstration an event, and criticism broader evaluation; protest is the closest.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) protest

व्याख्या: Remonstration गंभीर विरोध या आपत्ति की अभिव्यक्ति है।

Outrage भावना, demonstration आयोजन और criticism व्यापक आलोचना है; protest निकटतम है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q28', 28, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 28–30: Select the option closest to the opposite meaning of the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'Directions for questions 28–30: Select the option closest to the opposite meaning of the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'The advice rendered to him sounded to be quite SAGACIOUS.', 'The advice rendered to him sounded to be quite SAGACIOUS.', 'stupid', 'shallow', 'impracticable', 'insincere', 'stupid', 'shallow', 'impracticable', 'insincere', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) stupid

Explanation: Sagacious means wise or sound in judgement; stupid is its direct opposite.

Shallow, impracticable and insincere concern depth, feasibility and sincerity, not wisdom directly.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) stupid

व्याख्या: Sagacious विवेकपूर्ण या बुद्धिमान है; stupid सीधा विलोम है।

Shallow गहराई, impracticable व्यवहार्यता और insincere ईमानदारी से जुड़े हैं, सीधे बुद्धिमत्ता से नहीं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q29', 29, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 28–30: Select the option closest to the opposite meaning of the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'Directions for questions 28–30: Select the option closest to the opposite meaning of the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'The Indian cultural fair was held at Rome in a GRANDIOSE manner.', 'The Indian cultural fair was held at Rome in a GRANDIOSE manner.', 'unobtrusive', 'unimposing', 'unimpressive', 'simple', 'unobtrusive', 'unimposing', 'unimpressive', 'simple', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) simple

Explanation: Grandiose means elaborate or excessively grand; simple best contrasts with the manner described.

Unobtrusive concerns noticeability, while unimposing and unimpressive concern effect. Simple directly contrasts elaborate grandeur.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) simple

व्याख्या: Grandiose अत्यधिक भव्य या आडंबरपूर्ण है; simple सबसे उपयुक्त विपरीत है।

Unobtrusive ध्यान खींचने और unimposing/unimpressive प्रभाव से जुड़े हैं। Simple भव्य आडंबर का सीधा विपरीत है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q30', 30, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 28–30: Select the option closest to the opposite meaning of the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'Directions for questions 28–30: Select the option closest to the opposite meaning of the capitalised word in the sentence.', 'His voice sounded HAUGHTY when I spoke to him over the telephone.', 'His voice sounded HAUGHTY when I spoke to him over the telephone.', 'pleasant', 'humble', 'soft', 'cheerful', 'pleasant', 'humble', 'soft', 'cheerful', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) humble

Explanation: Haughty means arrogantly superior; humble means modest.

Pleasant, soft and cheerful describe attractiveness, volume or mood, not humility.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) humble

व्याख्या: Haughty घमंडी और humble विनम्र है।

Pleasant, soft और cheerful सुखदता, ध्वनि या मनोदशा बताते हैं, विनम्रता नहीं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q31', 31, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.salient_features_amendments_basic_structure', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Salient Features, Amendments & Basic Structure', 'Salient Features, Amendments & Basic Structure', 'Salient Features, Amendments & Basic Structure', 'Salient Features, Amendments & Basic Structure', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following statements is not correct?', 'कौन-सा कथन सही नहीं है?', 'The 42nd Amendment extended the term of Lok Sabha and State Legislative Assemblies from 5 years to 6 years.', 'The President can dissolve the Lok Sabha on the advice of the Prime Minister.', 'Money Bills cannot be introduced in the Rajya Sabha.', 'One third members of the Rajya Sabha retire on the expiry of every third year.', '42 वें संशोधन ने लोकसभा और राज्य विधानसभाओं का कार्यकाल 5 से 6 वर्ष किया।', 'राष्ट्रपति प्रधानमंत्री की सलाह पर लोकसभा भंग कर सकता है।', 'राज्यसभा में धन विधेयक पेश नहीं हो सकता।', 'राज्यसभा के एक-तिहाई सदस्य हर तीसरे वर्ष सेवानिवृत्त होते हैं।', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) One third members of the Rajya Sabha retire on the expiry of every third year.

Explanation: Rajya Sabha members serve six-year terms, with approximately one-third retiring every second year, not every third year.

The 42nd Amendment did make the extension in a, subsequently reversed by the 44th. Options b and c describe valid constitutional arrangements.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) राज्यसभा के एक-तिहाई सदस्य हर तीसरे वर्ष सेवानिवृत्त होते हैं।

व्याख्या: राज्यसभा का कार्यकाल छह वर्ष है और लगभग एक-तिहाई सदस्य हर दूसरे वर्ष सेवानिवृत्त होते हैं, तीसरे वर्ष नहीं।

a का विस्तार 42 वें संशोधन ने किया था, जिसे 44 वें ने पलटा। b और c सही संवैधानिक व्यवस्थाएँ हैं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q32', 32, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'history.ancient_india.post-gupta_period_harshavardhana', 'History', 'इतिहास', 'Ancient India', 'Ancient India', 'Post-Gupta Period & Harshavardhana', 'Post-Gupta Period & Harshavardhana', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'Ancient History', 'Indian History', 'Nalanda', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Nalanda University flourished during the reign of which of the following rulers?', 'किस शासक के समय नालंदा विश्वविद्यालय समृद्ध हुआ?', 'Chandragupta Maurya', 'Ashoka', 'Kanishka', 'Harsha', 'चंद्रगुप्त मौर्य', 'अशोक', 'कनिष्क', 'हर्ष', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) Harsha

Explanation: Harsha patronised Nalanda in the seventh century, when Xuanzang studied there.

The other rulers predate the flourishing Gupta/post-Gupta university described by the question; they are not the relevant patron among these choices.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) हर्ष

व्याख्या: सातवीं सदी में हर्ष ने नालंदा को संरक्षण दिया; उसी काल में ह्वेनसांग ने वहाँ अध्ययन किया।

अन्य शासक प्रश्न में वर्णित गुप्तोत्तर समृद्ध विश्वविद्यालय से पहले के हैं; दिए विकल्पों में संबंधित संरक्षक हर्ष है।', NULL),
