a, b, d के दक्षिणी/पश्चिमी मार्ग इस ऐतिहासिक सड़क का वर्णन नहीं हैं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q109', 109, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'history.indian_freedom_struggle', 'History', 'इतिहास', 'Indian Freedom Struggle', 'Indian Freedom Struggle', 'Indian Freedom Struggle', 'Indian Freedom Struggle', 'medium', ARRAY['Freedom Struggle', 'Modern Indian History', 'National Movement', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'The Civil Disobedience Movement of 1930 led to a1931 pact between Gandhi and', '1930 सविनय अवज्ञा के बाद 1931 में गांधी ने किससे समझौता किया?', 'Lord Irwin', 'Lord Linlithgow', 'Lord Wavell', 'Lord Curzon', 'लॉर्ड इरविन', 'लॉर्ड लिनलिथगो', 'लॉर्ड वेवेल', 'लॉर्ड कर्जन', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) Lord Irwin

Explanation: The Gandhi–Irwin Pact was signed in March 1931, leading to suspension of civil disobedience and Congress participation in the Second Round Table Conference.

Linlithgow and Wavell were later viceroys; Curzon served earlier. None signed the named 1931 pact.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) लॉर्ड इरविन

