    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q111', 111, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'art_culture_heritage.indian_literature_languages', 'Art, Culture & Heritage', 'कला, संस्कृति एवं विरासत', 'Indian Literature & Languages', 'Indian Literature & Languages', 'Indian Literature & Languages', 'Indian Literature & Languages', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Economy', 'General Studies', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Who wrote Algebra of Infinite Justice?', 'Algebra of Infinite Justice की लेखिका कौन हैं?', 'Anita Desai', 'Vikram Seth', 'Arundhati Roy', 'Rohinton Mistry', 'अनीता देसाई', 'विक्रम सेठ', 'अरुंधति रॉय', 'रोहिंटन मिस्त्री', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) Arundhati Roy

Explanation: The Algebra of Infinite Justice is Arundhati Roy’s collection of political essays.

Desai, Seth and Mistry are other novelists, not authors of this title.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) अरुंधति रॉय

व्याख्या: The Algebra of Infinite Justice अरुंधति रॉय के राजनीतिक निबंधों का संग्रह है।

देसाई, सेठ और मिस्त्री दूसरे उपन्यासकार हैं, इस पुस्तक के लेखक नहीं।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q112', 112, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.union_executive_state_executive.union_executive', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Union Executive & State Executive', 'Union Executive & State Executive', 'Union Executive (President - Election, Impeachment, Powers - Executive, Legislative, Financial, Judicial, Veto, Ordinance, Pardoning 72; Vice-President; Prime Minister & Council of Ministers - Collective Responsibility, Cabinet Committees)', 'Union Executive (President - Election, Impeachment, Powers - Executive, Legislative, Financial, Judicial, Veto, Ordinance, Pardoning 72; Vice-President; Prime Minister & Council of Ministers - Collective Responsibility, Cabinet Committees)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Who became President of India without first being Vice-President?', 'उपराष्ट्रपति रहे बिना कौन राष्ट्रपति बना?', 'V.V.Giri', 'R.Venkataraman', 'N.Sanjeeva Reddy', 'Zakir Hussain', 'वी.वी.गिरि', 'आर.वेंकटरामन', 'नीलम संजीव रेड्डी', 'जाकिर हुसैन', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) N.Sanjeeva Reddy

Explanation: N.Sanjeeva Reddy became President in 1977 without serving as Vice-President.

Giri, Venkataraman and Zakir Hussain had all held the vice-presidency before the presidency.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) नीलम संजीव रेड्डी

व्याख्या: नीलम संजीव रेड्डी 1977 में उपराष्ट्रपति रहे बिना राष्ट्रपति बने।

गिरि, वेंकटरामन और जाकिर हुसैन पहले उपराष्ट्रपति रहे थे।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q113', 113, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'general_mental_ability_quantitative_aptitude_comprehension.general_mental_ability_logical_reasoning', 'General Mental Ability, Quantitative Aptitude & Comprehension', 'सामान्य मानसिक योग्यता, मात्रात्मक अभिरुचि एवं बोधगम्यता', 'General Mental Ability & Logical Reasoning', 'General Mental Ability & Logical Reasoning', 'General Mental Ability & Logical Reasoning', 'General Mental Ability & Logical Reasoning', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Economy', 'General Studies', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'In a group of 36,16 take tea and 9 take tea but not coffee. How many take coffee but not tea?', '36 लोगों में 16 चाय और 9 चाय लेकिन कॉफी नहीं लेते हैं। केवल कॉफी कितने लेते हैं?', '27', '20', '25', '11', '27', '20', '25', '11', 'x', 'Correct Answer: Not established

Explanation: Seven drink both tea and coffee. But the 20 non-tea drinkers may include people drinking neither. Coffee-only therefore equals20 minus the unspecified neither group and cannot be determined.

Option b would be20 only if every member drinks at least one beverage, an assumption absent from the question. Options a, c exceed the 20 non-tea group; d is merely one possible value.', 'सही उत्तर: स्थापित नहीं

व्याख्या: सात दोनों पीते हैं। 20 चाय न पीने वालों में दोनों न पीने वाले भी हो सकते हैं। केवल कॉफी=20−अनिर्दिष्ट दोनों न लेने वाले; उत्तर निर्धारित नहीं।

b तभी 20 है जब हर व्यक्ति कम-से-कम एक पेय ले, जो नहीं दिया है। a, c,20 से अधिक हैं; d केवल एक संभावित मान है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q114', 114, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'general_mental_ability_quantitative_aptitude_comprehension.quantitative_aptitude_basic_numeracy.percentages_averages_ratio-proportion.percentages_successive_change', 'General Mental Ability, Quantitative Aptitude & Comprehension', 'सामान्य मानसिक योग्यता, मात्रात्मक अभिरुचि एवं बोधगम्यता', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution', 'General Studies', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'How many lines other than those shown in the octagon are required to join every corner with every other corner?', 'अष्टभुज में हर कोने को अन्य हर कोने से जोड़ने के लिए दिखाई भुजाओं के अतिरिक्त कितनी रेखाएँ चाहिए?', '56', '48', '20', '32', '56', '48', '20', '32', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) 20

Explanation: There are C(8,2)=28 distinct vertex pairs. Eight sides already exist, so20 diagonals remain.

56 double-counts ordered pairs; 48 and 32 do not subtract the eight existing edges from 28.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) 20

व्याख्या: C(8,2)=28 अलग शीर्ष-युग्म हैं। 8 भुजाएँ मौजूद हैं, इसलिए 20 विकर्ण चाहिए।

56 क्रमबद्ध युग्मों की दोहरी गिनती है;48,32 सही 28 से 8 घटाने के परिणाम नहीं हैं।', 'https://pub-254f3b08f36043179a6e58ed994fa499.r2.dev/questions/epfo/apfc-2002-q114.png'),
    ('epfo-apfc-2002-q115', 115, 2002, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'geography_earth_systems.indian_physical_geography_monsoon_architecture', 'Geography & Earth Systems', 'भूगोल एवं भू-प्रणाली', 'Indian Physical Geography & Monsoon Architecture', 'Indian Physical Geography & Monsoon Architecture', 'Indian Physical Geography & Monsoon Architecture', 'Indian Physical Geography & Monsoon Architecture', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Economy', 'General Studies', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Match city and river.
