    ('epfo-apfc-2004-q107', 107, 2004, NULL, 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_economy_development.macroeconomic_fundamentals_national_income_accounting', 'Indian Economy & Development', 'भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था एवं विकास', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution', 'General Studies', 'Indian Economy', 'Development']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Which statement is not correct?', 'कौन-सा कथन सही नहीं है?', 'Wellesley founded the first three Indian universities', 'Dalhousie introduced telegraph in India', 'Ripon introduced local self-government in towns and countryside', 'Curzon presided over Delhi Durbar 1903', 'वेलेजली ने पहले तीन भारतीय विश्वविद्यालय बनाए', 'डलहौजी ने भारत में तार शुरू किया', 'रिपन ने नगर और ग्रामीण स्थानीय स्वशासन शुरू किया', 'कर्जन ने 1903 दिल्ली दरबार की अध्यक्षता की', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) Wellesley founded the first three Indian universities

Explanation: Calcutta, Bombay and Madras universities were founded in 1857 under Lord Canning, not Wellesley.

b refers to Dalhousie’s telegraph expansion; c to Ripon’s 1882 local-government resolution; d to Curzon’s 1903 Durbar.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) वेलेजली ने पहले तीन भारतीय विश्वविद्यालय बनाए

