    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q19', 19, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'environment_ecology_disaster_management.climate_change_science_carbon_markets_global_conventions', 'Environment, Ecology & Disaster Management', 'पर्यावरण, पारिस्थितिकी एवं आपदा प्रबंधन', 'Climate Change Science, Carbon Markets & Global Conventions', 'Climate Change Science, Carbon Markets & Global Conventions', 'Climate Change Science, Carbon Markets & Global Conventions', 'Climate Change Science, Carbon Markets & Global Conventions', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'Environment', 'Biodiversity', 'Ecology', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'The Kyoto Protocol concerns what?', 'क्योटो प्रोटोकॉल किससे संबंधित है?', 'International trade', 'Deep-sea oil/mineral exploration', 'Clean environment and climate change', 'Common food stocks for disasters', 'अंतरराष्ट्रीय व्यापार', 'गहरे समुद्र में तेल/खनिज', 'स्वच्छ पर्यावरण और जलवायु परिवर्तन', 'आपदा के लिए साझा खाद्य भंडार', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) Clean environment and climate change

Explanation: The Kyoto Protocol under UNFCCC established greenhouse-gas emission commitments for developed countries.

Trade, seabed exploration and disaster food stocks are not this treaty’s subject.

Answer-key comparison: Independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series D key.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) स्वच्छ पर्यावरण और जलवायु परिवर्तन

