    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q21', 21, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'environment_ecology_disaster_management.biodiversity_wildlife_conservation_protected_areas', 'Environment, Ecology & Disaster Management', 'पर्यावरण, पारिस्थितिकी एवं आपदा प्रबंधन', 'Biodiversity, Wildlife Conservation & Protected Areas', 'Biodiversity, Wildlife Conservation & Protected Areas', 'Biodiversity, Wildlife Conservation & Protected Areas', 'Biodiversity, Wildlife Conservation & Protected Areas', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'Environment', 'Biodiversity', 'Ecology', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Why have vultures become rare in the countryside?', 'ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में गिद्ध दुर्लभ क्यों हुए?', 'Invasive species destroyed nesting sites', 'A drug used to treat cattle', 'Food scarcity', 'A widespread persistent fatal disease', 'बाहरी प्रजातियों ने घोंसले नष्ट किए', 'मवेशी उपचार की दवा', 'भोजन की कमी', 'व्यापक घातक रोग', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) A drug used to treat cattle

Explanation: Veterinary diclofenac residues in carcasses cause lethal kidney damage and visceral gout in susceptible vultures.

The principal documented crash was drug toxicity, not nesting invasion, simple food shortage or a contagious disease.

Answer-key comparison: Independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series D key.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) मवेशी उपचार की दवा

