    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q53', 53, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_polity_constitution_governance.fundamental_rights_dpsp_fundamental_duties.directive_principles_of_state_policy_-_part_iv_articles_36-51', 'Indian Polity, Constitution & Governance', 'भारतीय राजव्यवस्था, संविधान एवं शासन', 'Fundamental Rights, DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Fundamental Rights, DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Directive Principles of State Policy - Part IV / Articles 36-51 (Socialistic, Gandhian, Liberal-Intellectual Principles; Fundamental Rights vs DPSP Conflict & Harmony)', 'Directive Principles of State Policy - Part IV / Articles 36-51 (Socialistic, Gandhian, Liberal-Intellectual Principles; Fundamental Rights vs DPSP Conflict & Harmony)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, '“Protection of monuments and places and objects of national importance” is which provision?', '“राष्ट्रीय महत्त्व के स्मारकों, स्थानों और वस्तुओं की सुरक्षा” क्या है?', 'Fundamental Right', 'Directive Principle of State Policy', 'Fundamental Duty', 'Presidential order', 'मूल अधिकार', 'नीति निदेशक तत्व', 'मूल कर्तव्य', 'राष्ट्रपति आदेश', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) Directive Principle of State Policy

Explanation: Article 49 in Part IV directs state protection of nationally important monuments and objects.

It is not a Fundamental Right; Article 51A(f)’s cultural duty differs from this precise Article 49 wording; no presidential order is its constitutional source.

Answer-key comparison: Independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series D key.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) नीति निदेशक तत्व

