    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q65', 65, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'industrial_relations_and_labour_laws.labour_legislation_and_historic_acts.wages_legislation_acts', 'Industrial Relations & Labour Laws', 'औद्योगिक संबंध एवं श्रम कानून', 'Labour Legislation & Historic Labour Acts', 'Labour Legislation & Historic Labour Acts', 'Wages Legislation (Minimum Wages Act 1948 & Payment of Wages Act 1936)', 'Wages Legislation (Minimum Wages Act 1948 & Payment of Wages Act 1936)', 'medium', ARRAY['Minimum Wages', 'Payment of Wages', 'Bonus Act', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'The Minimum Wages Act 1948 chiefly safeguards workers in which sector?', 'न्यूनतम मजदूरी अधिनियम 1948 मुख्यतः किस क्षेत्र के श्रमिकों की रक्षा करता है?', 'Unorganised', 'Organised', 'Industrial', 'Agricultural', 'असंगठित', 'संगठित', 'औद्योगिक', 'कृषि', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) Unorganised

Explanation: Its core rationale is protection in scheduled employments where workers lack effective bargaining power, particularly the unorganised sector.

Industry and agriculture may be covered, but neither alone states the broad protective rationale; organised workers may have stronger bargaining institutions.

