    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q66', 66, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'indian_economy_development.macroeconomic_fundamentals_national_income_accounting', 'Indian Economy & Development', 'भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था एवं विकास', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'Macroeconomic Fundamentals & National Income Accounting', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'EPFO Verified PYQ']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'What expresses the relationship between market price and normal price?', 'बाजार कीमत और सामान्य कीमत का संबंध क्या है?', 'Market price is greater', 'Market price is equal', 'Market price tends towards normal price', 'Market price is lower', 'बाजार कीमत अधिक', 'बाजार कीमत बराबर', 'बाजार कीमत सामान्य की ओर जाती', 'बाजार कीमत कम', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) Market price tends towards normal price

Explanation: In the classical long-run account, competition and supply adjustment move fluctuating market prices towards normal price.

a and d are possible temporary deviations; b incorrectly treats equality as permanent.

