    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q84', 84, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'General English', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'A judgment made before all facts are known must be called what?', 'A judgment made before all facts are known must be called what?', 'Deliberate', 'Sensible', 'Premature', 'Harsh', 'Deliberate', 'Sensible', 'Premature', 'Harsh', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) Premature

Explanation: Premature means occurring before the appropriate time; a conclusion reached before adequate facts is premature.

Deliberate concerns intention; sensible reasonableness; harsh severity, none necessarily timing.

Answer-key comparison: Independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series D key.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) Premature

व्याख्या: Premature उचित समय से पहले है; पर्याप्त तथ्यों से पहले निष्कर्ष समयपूर्व है।

Deliberate इरादा, sensible विवेक और harsh कठोरता; कोई आवश्यकतः समय नहीं।

