    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q85', 85, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'General English', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Which pair matches ELUSIVE : CAPTURE?', 'Which pair matches ELUSIVE : CAPTURE?', 'Sensible : decide', 'Headstrong : controlled', 'Elastic : stretch', 'Persuasive : convince', 'Sensible : decide', 'Headstrong : controlled', 'Elastic : stretch', 'Persuasive : convince', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) Headstrong : controlled

Explanation: An elusive person is difficult to capture; a headstrong person is difficult to control. The relation is resistance to the stated action.

Sensible assists deciding, elastic permits stretching, persuasive helps convincing; none expresses resistance.

Answer-key comparison: Independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series D key.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) Headstrong : controlled

व्याख्या: Elusive व्यक्ति पकड़ना और headstrong व्यक्ति नियंत्रित करना कठिन। संबंध दिए कार्य का प्रतिरोध है।

