    ('epfo-apfc-2012-q86', 86, 2012, 'September', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['Indian Polity', 'Constitution of India', 'Governance', 'General English', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Choose the nearest opposite of “pursue” in “I wish I could pursue my studies.”', 'Choose the nearest opposite of “pursue” in “I wish I could pursue my studies.”', 'Discontinue', 'Abandon', 'Restrain', 'Deter', 'Discontinue', 'Abandon', 'Restrain', 'Deter', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) Discontinue

Explanation: Here pursue means continue or carry on studies; discontinue is the direct contextual opposite.

Abandon is a related stronger act of giving up, but discontinue most directly reverses continuing; restrain/deter concern holding back rather than ceasing studies.

Answer-key comparison: Independent answer matches the externally hosted UPSC-attributed Series D key.', 'सही उत्तर: (a) Discontinue

व्याख्या: यहाँ pursue पढ़ाई जारी रखना; discontinue उसका सीधा संदर्भगत विपरीत है।

Abandon पूरी तरह छोड़ना निकट पर अधिक तीव्र; discontinue सीधे जारी रखने को उलटता; restrain/deter रोकने से संबंधित हैं।

