    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q3', 3, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 1–5: Select the word or group of words most appropriate to fill the blank.', 'Directions for questions 1–5: Select the word or group of words most appropriate to fill the blank.', 'The dress isn''t really tight. It''ll _____ when you''ve worn it.', 'The dress isn''t really tight. It''ll _____ when you''ve worn it.', 'bend', 'expand', 'squeeze', 'stretch', 'bend', 'expand', 'squeeze', 'stretch', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) stretch

Explanation: Fabric stretches with wear, making a close-fitting dress less tight.

Bending concerns shape; squeezing compresses; expand is less idiomatic for a garment yielding through wear.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) stretch

