व्याख्या: Carnage व्यापक हत्या या रक्तपात है।

Lust तीव्र इच्छा, concern चिंता और satire व्यंग्य है; कोई नरसंहार नहीं बताता।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q12', 12, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'This RELIGIOUS gift, that makes men human, is still alive in Indian souls.', 'This RELIGIOUS gift, that makes men human, is still alive in Indian souls.', 'mystical', 'spiritual', 'metaphysical', 'philosophical', 'mystical', 'spiritual', 'metaphysical', 'philosophical', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) spiritual

Explanation: Spiritual most closely captures the connection with religion and the inner life in this context.

Mystical emphasises mystery, metaphysical abstract reality and philosophical general reasoning.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) spiritual

व्याख्या: इस संदर्भ में spiritual, धर्म और आंतरिक जीवन के संबंध को सबसे निकट व्यक्त करता है।

Mystical रहस्य, metaphysical अमूर्त वास्तविकता और philosophical सामान्य विचार-विमर्श पर बल देता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q13', 13, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'It is difficult for us to IMAGINE how much this safety means to everyone.', 'It is difficult for us to IMAGINE how much this safety means to everyone.', 'feel', 'understand', 'think', 'see', 'feel', 'understand', 'think', 'see', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) think

Explanation: The reference key uses think as the nearest offered word: imagine involves forming a mental conception.

Understand can also fit the sentence’s sense, but think is the retained scoring answer. Feel stresses emotion and see visual perception.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) think

व्याख्या: संदर्भ कुंजी think देती है; imagine का अर्थ मन में विचार या चित्र बनाना है।

Understand भी संदर्भ में उपयुक्त हो सकता है, लेकिन अंकन उत्तर think है। Feel भावना और see देखने को व्यक्त करता है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q14', 14, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'Public service is not merely something that occupies the hours you are doing it, but INVADES all your life and experience and affects them in one way or the other.', 'Public service is not merely something that occupies the hours you are doing it, but INVADES all your life and experience and affects them in one way or the other.', 'preserves', 'demolishes', 'covers', 'spoils', 'preserves', 'demolishes', 'covers', 'spoils', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) covers

Explanation: Invades is figurative here: public service permeates or covers the whole of one’s life.

Preserves protects; demolishes destroys; spoils damages. These do not express the stated pervasive influence.', 'सही उत्तर: (c) covers

व्याख्या: यहाँ invades लाक्षणिक है: लोकसेवा पूरे जीवन में व्याप्त होती है।

Preserves रक्षा, demolishes विनाश और spoils बिगाड़ना है; ये व्यापक प्रभाव नहीं बताते।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q15', 15, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.verbal_ability_sentence_rearrangement', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'Verbal Ability & Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles / Sentence Reordering - Identifying Opening Sentences, Connecting Links, Pronoun References, Concluding Sentences; Cloze Test - Contextual Word Fillers; Sentence Completion & Double Fillers)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'Directions for questions 11–15: Select the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word.', 'He was, in the early part of the twentieth century, a staunch nationalist of the LIBERAL fold.', 'He was, in the early part of the twentieth century, a staunch nationalist of the LIBERAL fold.', 'profuse', 'dogmatic', 'plentiful', 'tolerant', 'profuse', 'dogmatic', 'plentiful', 'tolerant', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) tolerant

Explanation: Liberal in this ideological sense suggests openness and tolerance of different views.

Profuse and plentiful concern abundance; dogmatic is rigid insistence and is closer to an opposite.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) tolerant

व्याख्या: वैचारिक संदर्भ में liberal खुले विचार और सहिष्णुता बताता है।

Profuse और plentiful प्रचुरता हैं; dogmatic कठोर आग्रह है और विपरीत अर्थ के निकट है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q16', 16, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.sentence_correction_spotting_errors', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Neither the servants nor the clerk has done this.', 'Neither the servants nor the clerk has done this.', 'Neither the servants', 'nor the clerk', 'has done this', 'No error', 'Neither the servants', 'nor the clerk', 'has done this', 'No error', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) No error

Explanation: With neither...nor, the verb agrees with the nearer subject clerk, which is singular; has is correct.

All three parts form a grammatical sentence. A plural verb is not required merely because servants appears first.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) No error

व्याख्या: Neither...nor में क्रिया निकटतम कर्ता clerk से मेल खाती है; एकवचन clerk के साथ has सही है।

तीनों भाग व्याकरणसम्मत हैं। पहले servants बहुवचन होने से यहाँ बहुवचन क्रिया आवश्यक नहीं होती।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q17', 17, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'The car which went past us when we were driving on the highway must have been doing at least a hundred miles an hour.', 'The car which went past us when we were driving on the highway must have been doing at least a hundred miles an hour.', 'The car which went past us', 'when we were driving on the highway', 'must have been doing at least a hundred miles an hour', 'No error', 'The car which went past us', 'when we were driving on the highway', 'must have been doing at least a hundred miles an hour', 'No error', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) No error

Explanation: The relative clause, past continuous time clause and modal perfect inference are all grammatical.

Doing a speed is idiomatic English. No listed part requires correction.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) No error

व्याख्या: संबंधवाचक उपवाक्य, भूतकालिक निरंतर समय-उपवाक्य और must have been का अनुमान सभी सही हैं।

Doing a speed अंग्रेजी का स्वाभाविक प्रयोग है। किसी सूचीबद्ध भाग में सुधार आवश्यक नहीं है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q18', 18, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.sentence_correction_spotting_errors', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Raju will be back home in an year after his stay abroad.', 'Raju will be back home in an year after his stay abroad.', 'Raju will be back home', 'in an year', 'after his stay abroad', 'No error', 'Raju will be back home', 'in an year', 'after his stay abroad', 'No error', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) in an year

Explanation: Year begins with the consonant sound /y/, so use a year rather than an year.

Parts a and c are acceptable; d is excluded by the article error in b.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) in an year

व्याख्या: Year व्यंजन ध्वनि /य/ से शुरू होता है, इसलिए a year होगा, an year नहीं।

भाग a और c सही हैं; b की article-संबंधी गलती के कारण d गलत है।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q19', 19, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.sentence_correction_spotting_errors', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'I have much work to do.', 'I have much work to do.', 'I have', 'much work', 'to do', 'No error', 'I have', 'much work', 'to do', 'No error', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) No error

Explanation: Work is uncountable, so much work is grammatically correct.

The infinitive to do modifies work appropriately. Many would require a countable plural noun.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) No error

व्याख्या: Work अगणनीय संज्ञा है, इसलिए much work व्याकरणतः सही है।

To do, work को सही ढंग से विशेषित करता है। Many के साथ गणनीय बहुवचन संज्ञा चाहिए।', NULL),
    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q20', 20, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.sentence_correction_spotting_errors', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Grammar', 'Vocabulary', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 16–20: Identify the erroneous underlined part (a), (b) or (c); choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Psychology did not develop into a science based of careful observation and experimentation until the late 1800s.', 'Psychology did not develop into a science based of careful observation and experimentation until the late 1800s.', 'Psychology did not develop into a science', 'based of careful observation', 'and experimentation until the late 1800s', 'No error', 'Psychology did not develop into a science', 'based of careful observation', 'and experimentation until the late 1800s', 'No error', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) based of careful observation

Explanation: The correct phrase is based on careful observation; based of uses the wrong preposition.

Parts a and c fit the corrected sentence. The error in b excludes no error.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) based of careful observation

व्याख्या: सही पदबंध based on careful observation है; based of में पूर्वसर्ग गलत है।

भाग a और c संशोधित वाक्य में सही हैं। b की गलती के कारण No error गलत है।', NULL)
