    ('epfo-eoao-2021-q75', 75, 2021, 'September', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'history.indian_freedom_struggle.revolt_of_1857.causes_of_the_revolt', 'History', 'इतिहास', 'Causes of the Revolt', 'Causes of the Revolt', 'Causes of the Revolt', 'Causes of the Revolt', 'medium', ARRAY['General Studies', 'EPFO', 'Freedom Struggle', 'Modern Indian History', 'National Movement']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Which was not recommended in Macaulay’s 1835 Minute on Education?', 'मैकॉले के 1835 के शिक्षा विवरण में कौन-सी सिफारिश नहीं थी?', 'Teaching in English medium', 'Liberal literary training', 'Teaching Western texts alone at higher levels of education', 'Teaching both Western and Oriental texts at higher levels of education', 'अंग्रेज़ी माध्यम में शिक्षण', 'उदार साहित्यिक प्रशिक्षण', 'उच्च शिक्षा में केवल पाश्चात्य ग्रंथों का शिक्षण', 'उच्च शिक्षा में पाश्चात्य और प्राच्य दोनों ग्रंथों का शिक्षण', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) Teaching both Western and Oriental texts at higher levels of education

Explanation: Macaulay favoured English-language education and European literature and science over state support for traditional Oriental learning. A balanced Western-and-Oriental higher curriculum was not his recommendation.

a, b and c align with the Anglicist educational approach; d describes the alternative it displaced.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) उच्च शिक्षा में पाश्चात्य और प्राच्य दोनों ग्रंथों का शिक्षण

