    ('epfo-eoao-2023-q6', 6, 2023, 'July', 1, 'eoao', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.reading_comprehension_sentence_correction_verbal_ability.sentence_correction_spotting_errors', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Reading Comprehension, Sentence Correction & Verbal Ability', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'Sentence Correction & Spotting Errors (Common Grammatical Errors - Dangling Modifiers, Redundancies, Misplaced Prepositions, Faulty Parallelism, Tense Inconsistencies, Double Negatives)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 6–10: Identify the erroneous part (a), (b) or (c). Choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Directions for questions 6–10: Identify the erroneous part (a), (b) or (c). Choose (d) if there is no error.', 'Ramesh liked his friend’s music player to his own.', 'Ramesh liked his friend’s music player to his own.', 'Ramesh liked', 'his friend’s music player', 'to his own', 'No error', 'Ramesh liked', 'his friend’s music player', 'to his own', 'No error', 'a', 'Correct Answer: (a) Ramesh liked

