    ('epfo-apfc-2023-q9', 9, 2023, 'July', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 6–10: Choose the option closest in meaning to the emphasized word.', 'Directions for questions 6–10: Choose the option closest in meaning to the emphasized word.', 'My SERENDIPITOUS encounter with the man on the bus was to have a profound impact on my life.', 'My SERENDIPITOUS encounter with the man on the bus was to have a profound impact on my life.', 'Fortunate', 'Of historical significance', 'Sudden and abrupt', 'A chance event', 'Fortunate', 'Of historical significance', 'Sudden and abrupt', 'A chance event', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) A chance event

Explanation: The key selects a chance event, capturing the unplanned encounter. Serendipitous more fully means a fortunate discovery by chance, so a captures another part of its meaning.

Historical significance and abruptness do not define serendipity; d preserves the scoring answer while acknowledging the overlap with fortunate.', 'सही उत्तर: (d) A chance event

