    ('epfo-apfc-2023-q51', 51, 2023, 'July', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'general_mental_ability_quantitative_aptitude_comprehension.quantitative_aptitude_basic_numeracy.percentages_averages_ratio-proportion.percentages_successive_change', 'General Mental Ability, Quantitative Aptitude & Comprehension', 'सामान्य मानसिक योग्यता, मात्रात्मक अभिरुचि एवं बोधगम्यता', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'Percentages, Successive Change & Base Effects', 'medium', ARRAY['Quantitative Aptitude', 'General Mental Ability', 'Arithmetic']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'Lenses of +2.0 D and −2.5 D are combined. The combination acts as what?', '+2.0 और −2.5 डायोप्टर लेंस साथ हों तो संयोजन क्या है?', 'Convex lens', 'Concave lens', 'Simple mirror', 'No image formation', 'उत्तल लेंस', 'अवतल लेंस', 'साधारण दर्पण', 'प्रतिबिंब नहीं बनता', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) Concave lens

Explanation: For thin lenses in contact, powers add: +2.0−2.5 = −0.5 D. Negative power is diverging, equivalent to a concave lens.

The result is not positive, reflective or zero-power, excluding the other choices.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) अवतल लेंस

व्याख्या: संपर्क में पतले लेंसों की शक्ति जुड़ती है: +2.0−2.5 = −0.5। ऋणात्मक शक्ति अपसारी, अर्थात अवतल समतुल्य है।

परिणाम धनात्मक, परावर्तक या शून्य शक्ति नहीं, इसलिए अन्य बाहर।', NULL),
    ('epfo-apfc-2023-q52', 52, 2023, 'July', 1, 'apfc', 'UPSC EPFO APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'science_technology_defence.applied_fundamental_sciences.applied_physics', 'Science, Technology & Defence', 'विज्ञान, प्रौद्योगिकी एवं रक्षा', 'Applied & Fundamental Sciences', 'Applied & Fundamental Sciences', 'Applied Physics (Wave Optics & Radiation - Refraction, Total Internal Reflection, Polarization, Dispersion, Lasers, LED vs OLED vs Sodium Lamps; Electromagnetic Spectrum - Gamma Rays, X-Rays, UV, Visible, Infrared, Microwaves, Radio Waves)', 'Applied Physics (Wave Optics & Radiation - Refraction, Total Internal Reflection, Polarization, Dispersion, Lasers, LED vs OLED vs Sodium Lamps; Electromagnetic Spectrum - Gamma Rays, X-Rays, UV, Visible, Infrared, Microwaves, Radio Waves)', 'medium', ARRAY['General Science', 'Physics & Chemistry', 'Biology']::TEXT[], NULL, NULL, 'In an inelastic collision in an isolated system, what is conserved?', 'पृथक तंत्र की अप्रत्यास्थ टक्कर में क्या संरक्षित है?', 'Kinetic energy, not momentum', 'Momentum, not kinetic energy', 'Both', 'Neither', 'गतिज ऊर्जा, संवेग नहीं', 'संवेग, गतिज ऊर्जा नहीं', 'दोनों', 'कोई नहीं', 'b', 'Correct Answer: (b) Momentum, not kinetic energy

Explanation: Total momentum is conserved without external impulse, while some kinetic energy becomes internal energy, deformation or heat.

c describes an elastic collision; a and d contradict momentum conservation in the isolated system.', 'सही उत्तर: (b) संवेग, गतिज ऊर्जा नहीं

