    ('epfo-eoao-apfc-2025-q9', 9, 2025, 'November', 1, 'eoao-apfc', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO & APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.idioms_phrases_phrasal_verbs', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'Idioms, Phrases & Phrasal Verbs (Popular Idiomatic Expressions with contextual meanings; Common Phrasal Verbs - Prepositional Verbs: Break down, Bring up, Call off, Carry out, Look into, Put up with, Turn down; Collocations in Business & Administrative English)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 6–10: Fill the blank with the most appropriate option.', 'Directions for questions 6–10: Fill the blank with the most appropriate option.', 'I was _____ exhausted by the end of the week spent in the library doing research work.', 'I was _____ exhausted by the end of the week spent in the library doing research work.', 'exceedingly', 'inordinately', 'very', 'completely', 'exceedingly', 'inordinately', 'very', 'completely', 'd', 'Correct Answer: (d) completely

Explanation: Exhausted is an extreme adjective, naturally intensified by completely to mean entirely worn out.

