    ('epfo-eoao-apfc-2025-q14', 14, 2025, 'November', 1, 'eoao-apfc', 'UPSC EPFO EO/AO & APFC', 'upsc-epfo', 'language_proficiency_grammar_communication.english_vocabulary_idioms_phrasal_verbs.lexical_building_blocks', 'Language Proficiency, Grammar & Communication (general Kannada & General English)', 'भाषा प्रवीणता, व्याकरण एवं संचार', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'English Vocabulary, Idioms & Phrasal Verbs', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'Lexical Building Blocks (Root Words: Greek & Latin roots; Prefixes & Suffixes; Synonyms & Antonyms; Homonyms, Homophones & Commonly Confused Words; One-Word Substitutions)', 'medium', ARRAY['General English', 'Language', 'Language Proficiency']::TEXT[], 'Directions for questions 11–15: Choose the option closest in meaning to the emphasized word.', 'Directions for questions 11–15: Choose the option closest in meaning to the emphasized word.', 'He abandoned his welfare beliefs after gaining wealth and was called an APOSTATE.', 'He abandoned his welfare beliefs after gaining wealth and was called an APOSTATE.', 'arrogant and haughty person', 'self-important person', 'renouncer of held beliefs', 'affluent person', 'arrogant and haughty person', 'self-important person', 'renouncer of held beliefs', 'affluent person', 'c', 'Correct Answer: (c) renouncer of held beliefs

